  "ground_truth": {
    "root_cause": "Deploy 9a8b7c6 repurposed the ROUTE_MODE feature flag. During the partial rollout (6 of 8 hosts), the two hosts still on the previous build (h7, h8) interpreted the same flag value as 'use the deprecated routing path', which contained a known bug that produced duplicate and malformed order submissions. About 12% of order flow - the share handled by the two stale hosts - went through the buggy legacy path. The trigger is deploying a semantic change to a shared flag without a coordinated cutover. Recovery required rolling back and disabling the legacy path.",
